# Rach2 clangd configuration (checked in).
#
# Run `sh tools/dev/gen_compile_commands.sh` to generate compile_commands.json
# (git-ignored) at the repo root; clangd reads it for each file's real compile
# flags. The kernel and the musl guest programs are built FREESTANDING with the
# i686-elf cross GCC, so clangd has to resolve THAT toolchain's headers
# (<stddef.h>, <stdint.h>, ...) and builtins, not
# the host's. clangd does that by querying the compiler named in the database, but
# only for drivers you allow, so launch clangd with:
#
#     --query-driver=**/i686-elf-*gcc
#
# (VS Code: set "clangd.arguments" to ["--query-driver=**/i686-elf-*gcc"]; other
# editors have an equivalent. See "clangd compilation database" in mk/Readme.md.)
#
# For the cross-compiled trees, pin the driver to the i686-elf cross GCC so clangd uses
# its freestanding headers even before the database is regenerated. The host krffs FUSE
# tools are left to their own (host cc) flags from the database.
If:
  PathMatch: [rach2/.*, tests/.*, ish/.*, utils/.*]
CompileFlags:
  Compiler: i686-elf-gcc
